# ⛔ Two things that look ignorable and are NOT — read before adding a line here.
#
#   suite/benchmark/manifest.json  the frozen task IDS and the hash they were read at.
#                                Committed on purpose: "frozen" has to be checkable by a
#                                stranger. ⛔ IDs and a hash — NEVER task bytes; vendoring
#                                the corpus makes us its owner again (D-062).
#                                ⚠️ This bullet used to name `truth.json`, our own answer
#                                key. D-062 moved the answer key upstream — it is now
#                                τ²'s `reward_breakdown` — so the file it argued about no
#                                longer exists in the design. A .gitignore comment is a
#                                claim like any other and nothing re-runs it.
#   uv.lock                      an application, not a library. A version table whose runs
#                                cannot be reproduced is a table of anecdotes.
#
# results/*.json and the spans under results/spans/ are committed too — they ARE the
# version table's evidence.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/

.env
.env.*

# the CLI's own checkpointer — per-machine state, not evidence (docs/06 §3)
.touchstone/

# ⛔ The phase-0 probes, and the reason they are ignored rather than kept: `doctor.py`
# is the productised version of exactly these checks, and it ships in src/. Two tools
# asking the same question is how one of them goes stale unnoticed — the same argument
# that retired the second index in this project's own docs. The probe output they
# produced is pasted verbatim in D-001 and docs/00 §6, so the *measurement* survives
# even though the scaffolding does not.
scripts/p0-*

# ⛔ The working record — local only. These are how the project steers itself; what it
# produces is README.md, docs/, diagrams/ and src/.
#
# ⚠️ The D-xxx, DEF-xxx and Pn.n tags in the published docs therefore resolve to nothing a
# reader can open — several hundred of them, including some baked into the rendered diagram's
# labels where no edit can reach them. That is deliberate: they mark where a choice was made, and
# README.md says so in one paragraph rather than leaving it to be discovered. ⛔ The rule that
# keeps this honest: if a reason is needed to understand the design, WRITE IT IN THE DOC. A
# tag is a bookmark, never a substitute for the argument.
#
# 🔴 Exact counts stood here — "176 decision citations, 22 defect ones, 54 phase ones, plus 15
# baked into the rendered diagram's labels" — and were removed on 2026-08-20 because no counting
# method reproduces them. Recounted over every tracked text file: 401 / 43 / 65 as occurrences,
# 50 / 21 / 20 as distinct ids, and narrowing to docs/ or excluding diagrams/README.md lands
# nowhere near either. Discarded rather than corrected: a census figure whose query was never
# recorded cannot be repaired, only replaced with a different unverifiable one. ⛔ And a count
# in a .gitignore comment is the worst possible home for one — nothing re-runs it, and it was
# doing no work here that "several hundred" does not do.
#
# scripts/check-diagram.py reads DECISIONS.md and DEFECTS.md, which is why it is local too —
# it could not run here even if it were published.
DECISIONS.md
DEFECTS.md
ROADMAP.md
scripts/check-diagram.py

# The local tracking store. D-074 made MLflow the spine with NO service, so the default
# tracking URI is a directory in this checkout — `mlruns/`, named in doctor.py:237 and
# docs/00 §the-stack. It did not exist as an ignore rule until 2026-08-21, which means the
# first real run would have dropped a trace store into the tree and the next `git add -A`
# would have committed it. The D-074 sweep read the docs and never read this file.
mlruns/

# Struck 2026-08-21. Phoenix had a docker volume; D-074 removed Phoenix, and D-040 had
# already removed the only other service, so there is no compose file left to own one.
# Kept as a line rather than deleted because a stale ignore rule is invisible either way,
# and the comment that was here asserted a container that does not exist.
.phoenix/

phase0.log
*.log

.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage

.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# ⛔ The D-068 node guard — local for a different reason from check-diagram.py above.
# It does not read the local-only registers; it hardcodes ABSOLUTE machine paths as its
# approved roots (this checkout, and the tau2-bench checkout beside it). Published, it
# would resolve nothing for anyone else and would read as a check that passes vacuously —
# which is the exact defect it was carrying on 2026-08-20, before the no-args guard.
scripts/check-diagram-nodes.sh

# ⛔ The session's own working directory. Machine-specific by construction — the settings
# file names absolute paths under /home/sandeep — so publishing it helps nobody and
# leaks the shape of a machine. This repo is PUBLIC; the working record stays local, the
# same rule the three registers above are ignored under.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
